e balances, including $10.6 billion at October 26, 2025."},{"ticker":"AMD","type":"circular_financing","summary":"The filings report AMD financing an ATMP joint venture that also supplies AMD and receives resale revenue from AMD."},{"ticker":"AMZN","type":"circular_financing","summary":"The filings report Amazon financing sellers through its seller lending program while also reporting seller receivables and seller activity as part of the commercial platform."},{"ticker":"ANET","type":"circular_financing","summary":"The filings report company financing of privately held companies that may also be counterparties to future customer or product-shipment agreements."},{"ticker":"ARM","type":"circular_financing","summary":"The company reports financing and revenue relationships involving related parties that also provide revenue or contract balances."},{"ticker":"AVGO","type":"off_balance_sheet","summary":"The Q2 FY2026 filing reports a backstop for a customer's lease obligations with maximum exposure of $29 billion."},{"ticker":"CRM","type":"circular_financing","summary":"The FY2026 filing reports Informatica revenue after the company financed part of the Informatica acquisition through associated credit facilities."}]},"categories":[{"label":"Cloud & platforms","tickers":["AMZN","GOOGL","IBM","META","MSFT","ORCL"],"ttm_revenue":1914882000000,"committed":700138000000,"wall_next5":3193476200000.0005},{"label":"Chips","tickers":["AMD","ARM","AVGO","INTC","MRVL","MU","NVDA","QCOM"],"ttm_revenue":568530700000,"committed":157223200000,"wall_next5":341295075850.08563},{"label":"Hardware & networking","tickers":["ANET","DELL","HPE","SMCI","VRT"],"ttm_revenue":228516606000,"committed":76317855000,"wall_next5":66467774613.40296},{"label":"AI software","tickers":["AI","CRM","NOW","PLTR","SNOW"],"ttm_revenue":68612032000,"committed":52058873000,"wall_next5":78087760312.92886},{"label":"Chip equipment","tickers":["AMAT","KLAC","LRCX"],"ttm_revenue":58656369000,"committed":24726971000,"wall_next5":23096301360.144005},{"label":"Data centers","tickers":["CRWV","DLR","EQIX","NBIS"],"ttm_revenue":24724308000,"committed":58762209000,"wall_next5":67155614166.66667}],"prose":{"intro":"This paper reviews 3889 filings from 31 companies in the industry. It covers filings through 2026-Q2 and uses data from 34 companies with pages. The filings show a large industry with $2.82 trillion in trailing-year revenue and major future commitments. They also show that reported totals can change when the records are reconciled.","debt":"The filings report $712.4 billion in debt. They report $1.05 trillion in total committed money. Total committed money is higher than reported debt, so debt alone does not capture all reported obligations.","revenue_reality":"The filings report $2.82 trillion in trailing-year revenue. They also report $237.9 billion in deferred revenue and $2.42 trillion in backlog. These figures distinguish revenue already recorded from revenue or obligations tied to future periods.","components":"The filings show revenue across Cloud & platforms, Chips, and Hardware & networking. These categories report $1.91 trillion, $568.5 billion, and $228.5 billion in trailing-year revenue. In 2025, reported spending included $974.4 billion in cost of revenue, $258.2 billion in research and development, $225.8 billion in sales and general administration, $121.6 billion in tax, and $302.2 billion in cash capital spending. Stock pay inside those expense lines was $117.0 billion.","wall":"The filings report $3.77 trillion of commitments due in the next 5y. They report $9.1 billion due in 5_to_10y and $4.6 billion beyond 10y. They also report $320.8 billion undated after year 5. Future revenue promised for the next 5y is $1.45 trillion.","growth":"The filings show revenue growth of 15% per year. Committed money grew 16% per year, while reported debt and deferred revenue each grew 14% per year. Median expense growth was 15% per year. On these reported measures, commitments grew faster than revenue, debt, and deferred revenue.","declared":"Reconciliation changed 303 of 802 quarters. The most common flag type was extraction disagreement, with 84 cases. Other leading types included subsequent event with 49, off balance sheet with 40, redefinition with 39, related party exposure with 34, and one time dressing with 27. These results show that reconciliation often changed the as filed numbers.","method":"The pipeline reads the filings, extracts reported values, and reconciles them across periods. Code owns the numerical calculations and comparisons. AI catalogs filing text and groups disclosures by type. The filings also report items such as purchase obligations, lease backstops, financing relationships, and related party commitments."}}